  body: |
    # Capital disregard evidence in the ESA(IR) source

    ## Authored interpretation

    The source places the capital-disregard question before valuation and requires evidence that the disregard applies.

    ## Scope and boundaries

    DMG 52351 carries Memo 11/20. Each disregard has its own conditions and period; this specific evidential burden is not assigned to every question. No current capital limit, tariff or award is adopted.

    ## Inspected source passages

    - [DMG 52351, PDF page 37](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f30ad3e08b8871b665ac/dmg-Ch-52.pdf#page=37)
    - [DMG 52352, PDF page 37](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f30ad3e08b8871b665ac/dmg-Ch-52.pdf#page=37)
    - [DMG 52353, PDF page 37](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f30ad3e08b8871b665ac/dmg-Ch-52.pdf#page=37)

    ## Evidence and review status

    This is an unreviewed, model-assisted interpretation of selected passages in the frozen DWP guidance. It is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable benefits rule. ESA(Cont), ESA(IR), New Style ESA, UC and Pension Credit are not equated. The captured source contains historical, transitional and potentially superseded provisions; no complete or current legal rule set is claimed. Machine extraction can affect reading order, footnotes and characters. No visual PDF review or specialist acceptance is claimed.

